intention:
  name: "The Hive's rules in tags with qh: (Quantum OS)"
  version: "1.0.0"
  category: "hive"
  goal: |
    Let a person declare, in one file, what the Hive of Quantum OS offers
    when something happens on the system and what its actuator may do at
    all, and get the two files the daemons load, with every promise in the
    file checked before anything runs.

  principles:
    - "One schema (quantum/runtime/hive/schema.py) is the language: a tag, an attribute, an event or an action it does not list is a compile error naming the line"
    - "Declarations only: there are no statements and no expressions; text where a tag goes is refused ('a hive file is declarations, not script')"
    - "A {field} is a field of the event the rule is on, of the right type, filled in by hive-synapse from the event itself and never from the model's text"
    - "An offer the file's own whitelist would refuse does not compile: the administrator never approves something that fails"
    - "The whitelist fails closed: what no <qh:allow> permits is denied, a <qh:block> wins over an allow, and rebooting, shutting down and suspending have no switch"

  capabilities:
    - "Declare, per event, the offers the dashboard shows and an administrator approves"
    - "Fill titles, descriptions and parameters from the event: the service, the unit, the port, the package, the mount"
    - "Permit commands argument for argument, services, paths, datasets, snapshot deletion and the switch-only permissions"
    - "Block services, packages and paths whatever is allowed"
    - "Bound how many of an action may run a minute"

  triggers:
    - '<q:application type="hive">'
    - "qh:on"
    - "qh:offer"
    - "qh:allow"
    - "the Hive's rules, the whitelist, what the Hive offers, what the actuator may do"

  structure: |
    <q:application id="hive" type="hive">
      qh:on event="..."              one rule per event
        qh:offer                     what an administrator may approve, with {field}s of the event
      qh:allow                       what the actuator may do: command= args=, service=, path=, dataset=, action=, delete-snapshot=
      qh:block                       what it may never do: service=, package=, path=
      qh:limit                       at most per-minute= of an action
    </q:application>

  semantics:
    # --- the tags ---
    - "qh:on holds the offers for one event (event=); one qh:on per event, its offers in order"
    - "qh:offer is one thing to approve: title= and description= (shown on the dashboard), action= (what runs) and the attributes that action takes; any of them may hold {field}"
    - "qh:allow permits one kind of thing: command= with args= (`*` is any one argument, the count must match), service= (names), path= (patterns), dataset= (patterns), action= (kill-port-process, open-url, firewall) or delete-snapshot= (a pattern)"
    - "qh:block forbids whatever is allowed: service= (patterns), package= (never removed; patterns) or path= (patterns)"
    - "qh:limit caps an action at per-minute= runs, under the actuator's overall limit"

    # --- the events, and their fields ---
    - "service-crash: a unit stopped unexpectedly; unit (nginx.service), service (nginx; absent when the unit is no .service, and the offers that need it are left out), exit_code"
    - "log-anomaly: a unit logs an unusual number of errors; unit, service"
    - "port-conflict: a program could not bind a port another holds; port, requester, holder"
    - "disk-low: a filesystem is nearly full; mount, percent, free_mb"
    - "memory-pressure: the system is low on memory; free_mb, total_mb"
    - "command-observed: a user ran a command the Hive judges dangerous; cmd, program"
    - "command-not-found: a user ran a program that is not installed and a package of that name exists; command, package (absent for an invalid name)"

    # --- the actions an offer may name (the kebab-case of hive-actuator's variants) ---
    - "run-command runs cmd= with args=; it must match a qh:allow command= of the file"
    - "start-service, stop-service, restart-service and reload-service act on service=, which must be allowed and not blocked"
    - "enable-service and disable-service set a service at boot, and act now unless now=false"
    - "install-package installs package= through PackageKit after a safety snapshot; any valid name, bounded by the limit"
    - "remove-package removes package= (never one a qh:block package= names), with purge=; dangerous, so the dashboard asks twice"
    - "update-package-lists, upgrade-packages (packages=, all when empty) and clean-package-cache take no name"
    - "kill-port-process ends the process on port= (a number, or a number field) with signal=; needs qh:allow action=\"kill-port-process\""
    - "create-snapshot snapshots dataset= as name= (recursive= true); list-snapshots lists dataset='s, or all; the dataset must match a qh:allow dataset="

    # --- what the files are ---
    - "rules.toml: the rules, every offer parameter a string, for hive-synapse, which also embeds the committed one as its built-in rules"
    - "whitelist.toml: hive-actuator's whitelist in the format it reads; version 2"
